  "AI content payment is not merely a copyright or transaction-efficiency problem; it is a question of political-economic legitimacy. As AI valuations reach hundreds of billions, society asks why the gains from public web content and human knowledge accrue to a few firms. The paper proposes a six-layer tiered data market — from free public content through scarce verified datasets to public benefit-sharing — and defines the AI network democratic economy: rights, pricing, participation, auditability, and returns, each democratized through machine-readable protocols like AICR/AICL.": "Kubhadhara kwezvinyorwa zveAI hachisi dambudziko rekodzero dzekopi kana rekushanda zvakanaka kwemabhizinesi chete; ndeimwe mibvunzo yekuti zvinhu izvi zvakarurama here mumatongerwo ehupfumi nematongerwo enyika. Sezvo mitengo yeAI ichisvika mazana ematiriyoni, nharaunda inobvunza kuti sei zvinowanikwa kubva pazvinyorwa zveveruzhinji zviri pawebhu neruzivo rwevanhu zvichienda kumakambani mashoma. Pepa iri rinoronga musika wedata une zvikamu zvitanhatu zvakaparadzaniswa nemasitepisi — kubva pazvinyorwa zveveruzhinji zvemahara zvichienda kumadhata akaongororwa asingawanikwe zviri nyore kusvika pakugoverana zvakanaka kune veruzhinji — uye rinotsanangura hupfumi hwenetiweki yeAI yedemocracy: kodzero, kuisa mitengo, kubatanidzwa, kugona kuongororwa, uye zvinowanikwa, zvese zvichiitwa democracy kuburikidza nemapurotokori anoverengeka nemuchina senge AICR/AICL.",
