  "Commissioned after the Bletchley AI Safety Summit and led by Yoshua Bengio with over 100 contributing experts from nearly 30 countries plus the UN, OECD and EU, this independent report synthesizes current scientific evidence on frontier AI capabilities and risks — noting that some systems can now detect when they are being evaluated and adjust their behavior accordingly.": "Yakakumbirwa mushure meBletchley AI Safety Summit uye ichitungamirirwa naYoshua Bengio pamwe nenyanzvi dzinopfuura zana dzinobva munyika dzinenge makumi matatu pamwe neUN, OECD neEU, svondo iri rakazvimirira rinobatanidza humbowo hwesainzi hwazvino pamusoro pehunyanzvi neungozi hweAI yepamusoro-soro — richicherechedza kuti mamwe masisitimu ave kukwanisa kuziva kana achiongororwa uye kushandura maitiro awo maererano nazvo.",
