  "Currency": "Mari",
  "Custom tier": "Chinhanho Chakagadzirwa",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nous inoshuma nezve chinyorwa chakatumirwa kuJournal of Medical Ethics chakadzoswa (retracted) chaive nezvinongedzo zvakagadzirwa, zveAI-hallucination zvakawanda — zvakazara nehukama hwemayunivhesiti enhema uye maadhiresi eemail asisashande — izvo zvinonzi munyori haana kugadzirisa kunyangwe mushure mekunge apihwa mukana wekugadzirisa mabhuku. Chinyorwa ichi chinoenzanisa izvi neBioethics, iyo kuongorora kwezvinongedzo kunoitwa nemuchina kwaizowana dambudziko racho, uye chinotaura kuti chinodzivirira chaicho hachisi tekinoroji yekuwana (script yemumwe akapa maonero yakaratidza zvinongedzo zvenhema mukati mechegumi chemineti) asi basa risingaripwe revaongorori uye zvikwambidzo zvekuburitsa zvinopa mubairo pakuwanda kwemabasa pane kunatsa kutarisisa.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Kutorera pasina muripo kwedata kuenzaniswa nemitengo yeAI inosvika matiriyoni",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabis akaronga mudzoreri wakafanana neFINRA wekuburitswa kwema-model epamusoro-soro: ma-lab aizotumira ma-model kuti aongororwe kusvika mazuva makumi matatu asati ashandiswa, kwokutanga zvichizviuya, nenzira inoenda kukuteerera kwakamanikidzwa mumusika weUS.",
  "Denied": "Zvakarambidzwa",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Chimiro chekutanga chemutemo chinogona kuiswa",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Chimiro chekutanga chemutemo chinogona kuiswa chiri pa/downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — saiti diki yakamira ine chinyorwa chakazara chinoverengeka nemuchina, yakagadzirira Cloudflare Pages kana chero static host.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Kuisa mitemo inoverengeka nemuchina pasaiti yenyu",
  "Disclaimer": "Ziviso",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "Yakasiyana neUI yevanhu, SEO, kana maAPI akangojairika, AI Ingestion & Capability Layer inopa mawebsite chimiro chakatarisana nemuchina: Manifest Layer (nzira dzekupinda senge /llms.txt ne/ai/manifest.json), Corpus Layer (ruzivo runoverengeka nemuchina), Capability Layer (zvishandiso zvinodaidzwa neagent), uye Governance Layer (provenance, rezinesi, vhezheni). Inotanga nestatic, inogona kukwidziridzwa kuenda kumaAPI neMCP. Cherechedza: mupepa iri AICL rinoreva chimiro chekutora zvinyorwa; pamapeji emapurotokori esaiti ino AICL rinoreva AI Content Licensing Layer.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Zvinyorwa",
  "Docs / Examples": "Zvinyorwa / Mienzaniso",
  "Document library": "Raibhurari yeZvinyorwa",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "AI ine kodzero here — uye ndeapi maonero anonyatsobatana?",
  "Download": "Dhawunirodha",
