  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Muenzaniso wekudzidzisa: HMAC-SHA256 ine chakavanzika chakagoverwa, ichiratidza matoken erezinesi akasungirirwa kuchikumbiro, ane nguva yekupera, uye anogona kusimbiswa. Matoken echaizvo anofanira kusainwa neasymmetric, iyo kiyi yeveruzhinji yemuburitsi ichiwanikwa pasi pe/.well-known/.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Zvimwe zvinyorwa zvisere zve/topics, panguva ino zvakatsvakwa neAI agent pane kusarudzwa nemaoko — mutemo mumwechete sepakutanga: source imwe neimwe inotorwa uye inosimbiswa kuti iripo, zvipfupiso zvakanyorwa nemamwe mazwi ekutanga, zvisati zvawedzerwa. Zvinyorwa gumi nezvina pamwe chete.",
